WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.840
- There's a popular saying that goes,

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.680
if Britney survived 2007,
you can survive today.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.870
But what contributed to her
public and private struggles,

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.470
and what can we learn from
her trials and tribulations

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.310
that have contributed to pop
culture as we know it today?

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.523
We're about to find out.

00:00:15.523 --> 00:00:17.680
(electronic dance music)

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.970
We've got a panel of
Britney experts here today,

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.800
ranging from diehard
Stans to people who have

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.610
a more complicated
relationship with the pop star.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.780
We have like, a spectrum here, it's like.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.613
- Straight to gay.

00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:31.490
- Exactly.
(panel laughs)

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.270
Who is Britney Spears?

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.640
She was born on a holy
day, December 2, 1981

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.620
in Kentwood, Louisiana to
Jamie and Lynne Spears.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.400
At age 11, Britney is accepted
into the Mickey Mouse Club,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.120
and she goes on to sign with Jive Records

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.010
and becomes an opening act for N'SYNC.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.910
Britney became a star pretty quickly.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.150
In 1998, at the age of 17,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.850
she released "Baby One More Time."

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.670
The album Baby One More Time

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.000
became the biggest-selling
LP by a teenage artist ever.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.350
- I think the music video
is what made it go crazy.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.540
- The whole video was her idea,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.420
the whole like, school room thing.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.890
She tied up her shirt all on her own.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.610
She was in charge of
her vision from day one.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.450
I was officially a gay man.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.450
- I think that's very
smart, but I love the way

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.580
how you said, she pulled
up and tied her shirt

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.420
as if she like, fucking solved gravity.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.560
- That was so iconic,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.470
tell me you didn't do that at this age.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.730
- No, it's iconic, but people
did that before her, too.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:23.798
- I mean, we're still talking about it.

00:01:23.798 --> 00:01:25.020
- True, true.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:25.940
- [Sam] There's no argument.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.940
She became the biggest
pop star in the world.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.500
From the beginning, the media has always

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.855
had a fascination with
Britney's sexuality.

00:01:31.855 --> 00:01:34.181
In 2000, at the MTV Movie Awards,

00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:37.580
Britney ripped away a black suit to reveal

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.840
a crystal nude body suit,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.760
which was considered
controversial at the time

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.550
because she was only 19 years old.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.030
- Girl Scout moms in my group thought

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.800
she was a bad role model.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.440
- She once again sparked
controversy at the 2001 VMAs

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.350
when she performed scantily-clad

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.590
with a python wrapped
around her shoulders.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.080
Also, this huge speculation

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.610
over her first public relationship

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.350
with the infamous Justin Timberlake.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.690
You guys remember their AMAs outfit

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.770
where they were dressed
in all denim, right?

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:08.786
- [Sheridan] Who doesn't
remember that outfit?

00:02:08.786 --> 00:02:09.650
(panel laughs)

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.610
That will go in like, a museum.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.810
- [Sam] The media was instantly infatuated

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.100
with their relationship.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.530
But the fairy tale was not meant to last.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.930
Britney and Justin broke up in 2002.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:22.330
It was rumored they split
because Britney was cheating,

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.730
and she never directly
denied these allegations.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.170
- Justin really wants you to know

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.540
that Britney cheated on him.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.020
- [Sheridan] Cry Me a River
was his huge first song.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.000
- [Christian] Because of what?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.010
- [Sheridan] Britney,
it was about Britney.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.130
- [Christian] He put this
woman with blonde hair,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.640
gave her that pink hat,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.360
and he made it into his first big hit,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.280
and that pushed him into pop stardom.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.714
Before that, he was
just a member of N'SYNC.

00:02:45.714 --> 00:02:48.440
- I want to know what Jessica
Biel thinks about this.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.780
- Right? I don't know.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.514
- She's too busy running Au Fudge.

00:02:51.514 --> 00:02:53.160
(panel laughs)

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.800
Justin publicly stated that
during their relationship

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.430
they had sex, which was a big deal,

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.040
