and Spears' visitation
rights with her children

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.730
were also suspended until she complied

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.010
with court orders in their custody battle.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.690
After she was asked how she was doing,

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.350
Spears was filmed telling reporters,

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:13.980
quote, "Eat it, snort
it, lick it, fuck it."

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.010
And she's also speaking
in a British accent

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.900
to paparazzi at this time.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.758
In the midst of all this personal drama,

00:10:20.758 --> 00:10:24.660
Britney's team strong-armed her
into performing at the VMAs.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.250
- Obviously, the performance of someone

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.760
who was struggling with a lot of stuff.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:29.170
- [Sam] For the performance,
she had to wear a wig

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.730
because her hair was still growing back.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.040
- She stayed out until
2:30 a.m. that night.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.715
- Forget appearance,
because people have made

00:10:34.715 --> 00:10:37.537
comments about her not
being in peak shape.

00:10:37.537 --> 00:10:39.550
She looked downright out of it.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.270
- Was she ever going to win over

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.600
the general public at that point?

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.802
I mean, we were in the middle
of lighting her on fire.

00:10:45.802 --> 00:10:47.810
- They wanted that to happen.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.860
- Despite all these person struggles,

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.020
in 2007, Britney manages to release

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:56.920
quite possibly her best
album yet, Blackout.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.350
- A piece of light in
a very dark, dark time.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.590
- [Pablo] I think, after
seeing headline after headline

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.770
being like her career's
over, her career's over,

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:04.690
her fans were over her,

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.850
she still releases a good body of work.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.880
- It was her only album
to join the archives

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.600
of the Rock &amp; Roll Hall of Fame.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.490
After Blackout's release,
Britney Spears was hospitalized

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:15.070
after locking herself in the bathroom

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.969
with her youngest son,
Jayden, for three hours,

00:11:16.969 --> 00:11:18.760
and refusing to hand him over

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.730
to her ex-husband Kevin Federline.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.230
Later in the month, Britney
Spears is hospitalized again,

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:26.286
and a motorcade of police
vehicles and a police helicopter

00:11:26.286 --> 00:11:29.370
took her in an ambulance at 1 a.m.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.150
Her mother also encouraged Dr. Phil

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.330
to visit Britney in the Psychiatric Ward

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.380
of Cedars-Sinai Medical
Center at this time.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.020
Dr. Phil immediately went around

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:38.650
and told the press everything.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.480
In 2008, Britney Spears begins

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:42.150
being controlled by a guardianship,

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.240
a court approved
conservatorship for people

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:47.190
who are deemed incapable of
taking care of themselves.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.610
This is a major turning point in her life.

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:52.230
- I think why she committed
to the conservatorship

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.230
was so she could have
some custody of her kids,

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.560
so she could see her kids.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.090
- All she cared about was her children.

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.356
- There's a lot of good
things that can come

00:12:00.356 --> 00:12:03.370
out of structure and some certain limits.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.580
- She went into hiding a bit.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:06.820
You didn't see her everywhere.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.660
You didn't see all these
Britney controversies.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.950
It's gets sticky when
you think about her dad

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:13.290
and the money he makes
from being a conservator.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.123
- [Sheridan] If she's being forced

00:12:14.123 --> 00:12:16.970
into a studio at
gunpoint, we have no idea.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:17.860
- And they're priming her up

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.040
for this huge comeback at the 2008 VMAs,

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.410
a year after the "Gimme More" performance.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.640
- [Sheridan] Was it really only a year?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.570
- Only a year.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.290
Was it too soon for her?

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:29.890
- Hopefully, their cycle
just doesn't repeat itself

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.530
where she feels like too many people

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.150
are around her and controlling her.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:37.670
- If what happened in
Britney's career in 2007

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:41.750
happened today in 2018, how
would it play out differently?

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.330
- People are way more empathetic

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.220
to issues surrounding mental health.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.370
- I will say that sometimes

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.460
I feel like people still
haven't even learned this

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.410
because if you you look at
Amanda Bynes in her time,

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.720
there was the same exact process.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.480
None of us want to be watched like that,

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.970
so I don't understand why
you can watch someone,

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:03.860
laugh at them, but I'm
gonna go mess up in private

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.420
because I have that ability to.

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:07.030
- Do you guys think we made any progress

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.200
in the way that media treats and portrays

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.050
women's bodies and sexuality?

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.360
- Now we're in a place where
we're talking about it,

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.150
and people are admitting
things and being vocal.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:21.520
I see, as time goes on, we're
reclaiming our sexuality

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:25.560
and trying to figure out
what it means to be a woman.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:29.310
I think we can describe
Britney as a trailblazer.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:32.160
She could have just
crawled back to Louisiana,

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.060
and we would be talking about,

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.160
like, whatever happened to Britney Spears.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.750
But the mere fact that she came back

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.030
and stronger than ever
is pretty impressive.

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:43.570
Before her, Vegas was
seen as you're getting

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:47.230
a little older as an artist,
have a Vegas residency,

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:49.600
get some good money in your last years.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.600
Britney turned that into you can go

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:56.230
while you're still the
young artist you are,

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.820
make good money, people will come see you

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:00.076
from all around the world.

00:14:00.076 --> 00:14:03.230
And now, look, everyone's coming to Vegas.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.400
- Yeah.
- She is a trailblazer,

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.570
so it's exciting to see.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.180
She's only 35, 36.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.110
- Which I think is the
age that you qualify

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:13.400
to run for President of the United States.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.678
- I can't handle that.

00:14:15.678 --> 00:14:17.482
(panel laughs)

00:14:17.482 --> 00:14:22.482
("America the Beautiful"
by Katharine Lee Bates)

